 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "dependencies lists distinct [caller, callee] pairs of service names forming a directed acyclic graph (no self edges). When a service receives one unit of load it sends one unit to each of its callees, so the load factor of a service equals the number of distinct call paths from entry to it (entry itself has 1). Return [service, loadFactor] for every service named in dependencies or as entry, sorted by name; services that entry cannot reach have 0. Every load factor is at most 2**53 - 1.",
  "provenance": [
   {
